  "query_preview": "/Through Sunday/...\nIssued at 1155 AM MST Sun Nov 8 2026\n\nAn upper level ridge will continue to bring sunny skies, light \nwinds, and well above normal temperatures through Monday. Cross \nsections show the airmass will stay very dry with only some cirrus\nclouds at times. High temperatures will run 10F to 15F above \nnormal with highs in the mid to upper 60s across northeast \nColorado. Even a few low 70s will be possible.\u00a0\n\nA shortwave trough will pass north of Colorado on Tuesday. The \nGFS model has been trending more south with the shortwave trough's\ntrack compared to the other models, and it continues to do so but\nthe latest run shows a northward shift. This system will bring \ngusty west to northwest winds to northern Colorado Tuesday and \nTuesday night.\u00a0 A weak cold front will also accompany this system,\nleading to slightly cooler temperatures for Wednesday. High \ntemperatures on Wednesday are expected to be in the upper 50s to \nlower 60s.\u00a0 No precipitation is expected with this system.\u00a0\n\nThe upper level ridge reestablishes itself over the Intermountain\nWest on Thursday. Northerly flow aloft will prevail over Colorado\nwith temperatures reaching the lower to mid 60s. The ridging\nslides east and will center over the Central Rockies for Friday\nand Saturday. This is expected to push temperatures back into the\nmid to upper 60s across northeast Colorado. A few low 70s will\nalso be possible. The ridge slides east of the region by Sunday as\na shortwave trough moves across the Desert Southwest. Dry\nconditions are expected to persist Sunday under a dry southwest\nflow aloft. Temperatures will continue to run well above average\n(10-15F).",
